id: bluetooth_agents_controller
label: Bluetooth controller agents.md contributions
package: bluetooth_le_controller
description: >
  Bluetooth Controller usage contributions for agents.md
category: Bluetooth|Bluetooth LE Controller (Link Layer)
quality: evaluation
provides:
- name: bluetooth_agents_controller
template_contribution:
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_controller
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_controller
    context: |
      # Bluetooth Controller for Silicon Labs Series 2 and Series 3 devices
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_hci
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_hci
    context: |
      ## HCI
      - This is for applications that do not use the SiSDK `bluetooth_stack`.
        Supported commands and features depend on the controller components included by the application.
        Query local supported commands/features using HCI_Read_Local_Supported_Commands and
        HCI_LE_Read_Local_Supported_Features_Page_0.
      - UART is the default transport. CPC and 3-wire are available alternatives.
      - Unavailable to SoC and NCP applications that use the SiSDK `bluetooth_stack` and BGAPI.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_advertiser
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_advertiser
    context: |
      ## Advertising
      - Set advertising parameters and data before start.
      - Max advertising interval: 0xFFFF × 0.625 ms = 40959.375 ms; larger
        values are rejected.
      - Legacy advertising: advertising data and scan-response data are each limited to 31
        bytes; longer data is rejected. Scannable advertising can put extra
        payload in the scan response.
      - Extended advertising can only be one of connectable, scannable, or non-connectable and
        non-scannable. Data may be up to 1650 bytes and must fit within one advertising interval or
        advertising is rejected.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_scanner
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_scanner
    context: |
      ## Scanning
      - Before starting scanning, set scanning parameters.
        Duty cycle = scanning window / scanning interval (maximum 100%).
      - At high duty cycle, slow consumption of advertising reports can
        exhaust controller buffers and throttle the system; drain reports
        promptly or use filtering.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_connection_role_central
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_connection_role_central
    context: |
      ## Central connection
      - Scan for connectable advertisers, then create a connection by address.
      - PHY update is opt-in: include `bluetooth_feature_connection_phy_update`
        (not present by default, to save flash and memory).
      - Max number of connections is 32, or fewer based on available memory.
        If the goal is lowest latency, use `bluetooth_controller_anchor_selection`.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_connection_role_peripheral
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_connection_role_peripheral
    context: |
      ## Peripheral connection
      - Start connectable advertising; scannable-only advertising never
        establishes a connection.
      - When a connection is established, the controller stops that
        advertising set.
      - PHY update is opt-in: include `bluetooth_feature_connection_phy_update`.
      - Max number of connections is 32, or fewer based on available memory.
      - The central owns connection timing; peripherals cannot freely
        reschedule, so multi-connection scaling needs careful interval and
        timeout design.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_cs
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_cs
    context: |
      ## Channel Sounding
      - Channel Sounding is only supported on devices with CS-capable hardware.
      - Before starting CS procedures: exchange CS capabilities, enable CS security,
        create a CS configuration, then set procedure parameters.
      - Subevent length is negotiated by the link layers; the application
        cannot preset it.
      - CS SYNC PHY (mode 0, mode 1 and RTT portion of mode 3) is different from
        the connection PHY; CS SYNC PHYs and device-supported PHYs may differ.
      - CS needs larger Bluetooth buffers and, on HCI/UART paths, a higher
        baud rate to deliver subevent results; otherwise subevent aborts are
        more frequent.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_sync
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_sync
    context: |
      ## Periodic advertising sync
      - Scan to discover periodic advertisers before creating a sync.
      - Sync can also be established via PAST if `bluetooth_feature_sync_past`
        (and related PAST components) are included.
      - If sync is lost (for example, on timeout), the application must recreate it.
      - Max number of simultaneous syncs depends on memory. Independent periodic
        advertisers can overlap in time and cause scheduling conflicts or
        missed events.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_hci_sleep
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_hci_sleep
    context: |
      ## HCI sleep
      - Vendor-specific sleep puts the controller into EM2; without a sleep
        command the device stays at EM1 when idle.
      - Not supported with CPC transport.
      - After a sleep command, wake is driven by activity on the HCI UART RX
        pin; call `sl_btctrl_hci_sleep_sleep()` from the normal process loop
        (the component wires this) so the wake path can complete and send the
        command-complete event.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_connection_phy_update
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_connection_phy_update
    context: |
      ## Connection PHY update
      - Optional component: without it, connections stay on the default 1M
        PHY. Include this component to configure a preferred PHY other than 1M
        (for example 2M or coded).
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_sync_past
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_sync_past
    context: |
      ## PAST — transfer established sync
      - Use to transfer synchronization info for an **established** periodic
        sync to a peer over a connection.
      - For a **local** periodic advertising set, use
        `bluetooth_feature_advertiser_past` instead.
      - To **receive** PAST, use `bluetooth_feature_past_receiver`.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_advertiser_past
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_advertiser_past
    context: |
      ## PAST — transfer local advertising set
      - Use to transfer synchronization info for a **local active** periodic
        advertising set to a peer over a connection.
      - For an **established** sync, use `bluetooth_feature_sync_past` instead.
      - To **receive** PAST, use `bluetooth_feature_past_receiver`.
- name: agents_slab
  condition:
  - bluetooth_feature_past_receiver
  priority: -5300
  value:
    id: bluetooth_feature_past_receiver
    context: |
      ## PAST — receive
      - Use on the device that **receives** Periodic Advertising Sync Transfer
        over a connection.
      - To initiate PAST, use `bluetooth_feature_advertiser_past` and/or
        `bluetooth_feature_sync_past` on the sender.

ui_hints:
  visibility: never

metadata:
  sbom:
    license: MSLA
root_path: bluetooth_le_controller
